## 28. AI VOICE RESPONSE LOOP REPAIR

Treat the previously observed repetitive voice response loop as a critical release blocker.

Repair the underlying runtime failure before expanding the AI Front Desk.

Investigate:

- Repeated network recovery responses.
- Incorrect API endpoint configuration.
- Frontend/backend version mismatch.
- Gemini provider availability.
- WebSocket handshake failures.
- Speech recognition duplication.
- Microphone echo.
- Assistant self-transcription.
- Duplicate playback.
- Stale responses.
- Uncontrolled reconnection.

Implement:

- Centralized voice state machine.
- Unique conversation turn identifiers.
- Duplicate suppression.
- Stale response rejection.
- Bounded retry budgets.
- Circuit breaker.
- Echo cancellation.
- Controlled audio playback.
- Reliable session cleanup.
- Manual retry controls.
- Verified text fallback.

Never repeatedly speak the same network error.

Stop automatic recovery when the failure budget is exhausted.

Do not claim voice functionality is operational until actual hosted acceptance passes.

